      "narrative": "Mara's eyebrow lifts at the shift in your question. She sets down her cup, the clay clinking against the wood.\n\n\"That's a more interesting question than the last one.\" She gestures with her chin toward the far end of the taproom, where a nervous figure sits hunched over a stack of papers, ink-stained cuffs peeking from beneath his coat sleeves.\n\n**Toran Vex** looks up as if he felt the weight of her gaze. He's a thin man, pale, with the twitchy energy of someone who expects bad news at any moment.\n\n\"Toran there,\" Mara says, lowering her voice. \"He was the lockwright for the Kestrel Guild. Maintained the Ash Gate's mechanism for years before it was sealed. If anyone knows what was done to that lock \u2014 and who filed it shut \u2014 it's him.\"\n\nToran's quill has stopped moving. He's watching you both now, his throat bobbing as he swallows.\n\n\"He doesn't talk about it much,\" Mara adds, a dry edge to her voice. \"But he's here. And he's listening.\"\n\nToran clears his throat, voice thin. \"You... you have questions about the Gate?\""
    },
