      "narrative": "A log shifts in the hearth, sending a brief flare of light across the room. Mara Venn's fingers tighten around her cup as she considers you, her sharp eyes unreadable.\n\n\"Who sold passage,\" she repeats, testing the words. She lets out a breath. \"Old Bram handled the coin, but he wasn't the one who authorized it. The Gate was never his to open freely \u2014 he took orders.\"\n\nShe leans forward, voice dropping to nearly a murmur. \"The name you want is **Sable Quill**. A courier in a travel-stained cloak. She carried the writs, collected the tariffs, and decided who crossed and who didn't. She was the Gate's keeper in all but title.\"\n\nMara holds your gaze. \"She's still alive, far as I know. Hasn't been seen in months, but she hasn't been found dead either. Last anyone heard, she was still haunting the Gate's shadow.\"\n\nShe tilts her head. \"That the name you were after?\"\n\nThe answer is there \u2014 the who, the role, the thread \u2014 but the *where* and *why* remain coiled just out of reach. You have a name. Now what do you do with it?"
    },
